      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n   size_t length;\n} string_info;\n\nlong int* bucket_sort(char *a, int length, long int size, int offset, int nbuckets) {\n   long int *returns;\n   long int *scratch;\n   long int *source;\n   long int *destination;\n   string_info *info;\n   size_t max_length = 0;\n\n   /* The original bucket ordering is the same as global bytewise ordering. */\n   (void)offset;\n   (void)nbuckets;\n   if (size <= 0)\n      return NULL;\n\n   returns = (long int *)malloc(sizeof(long int) * (size_t)size);\n   scratch = (long int *)malloc(sizeof(long int) * (size_t)size);\n   info = (string_info *)malloc(sizeof(string_info) * (size_t)size);\n   if (returns == NULL || scratch == NULL || info == NULL) {\n      free(returns);\n      free(scratch);\n      free(info);\n      return NULL;\n   }\n\n   for (long int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n      const char *token = a + (size_t)i * (size_t)length;\n      info[i].length = strlen(token);\n      if (info[i].length > max_length)\n         max_length = info[i].length;\n      returns[i] = i;\n   }\n\n   source = returns;\n   destination = scratch;\n\n   /* Stable LSD passes, with NUL padding so variable-length tokens sort like strcmp. */\n   for (size_t position = max_length; position > 0; position--) {\n      size_t counts[257] = {0};\n      size_t byte_position = position - 1;\n\n      for (long int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n         size_t index = (size_t)source[i];\n         unsigned int digit = 0;\n         if (byte_position < info[index].length) {\n            const unsigned char *token = (const unsigned char *)\n               (a + index * (size_t)length);\n            digit = (unsigned int)token[byte_position] + 1U;\n         }\n         counts[digit]++;\n      }\n\n      size_t next = 0;\n      for (size_t digit = 0; digit < 257; digit++) {\n         size_t count = counts[digit];\n         counts[digit] = next;\n         next += count;\n      }\n\n      for (long int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\n         size_t index = (size_t)source[i];\n         unsigned int digit = 0;\n         if (byte_position < info[index].length) {\n            const unsigned char *token = (const unsigned char *)\n               (a + index * (size_t)length);\n            digit = (unsigned int)token[byte_position] + 1U;\n         }\n         destination[counts[digit]++] = source[i];\n      }\n\n      long int *tmp = source;\n      source = destination;\n      destination = tmp;\n   }\n\n   if (source != returns)\n      memcpy(returns, source, sizeof(long int) * (size_t)size);\n\n   free(scratch);\n   free(info);\n   return returns;\n}\n\nvoid load(char **vString, long int *N, int *l, int *os, int *nb){\n   char *strings = NULL;\n   int      len,\n            offset,\n            nbucket;\n   long int n;\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &len)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR len\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%ld\", &n)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR n\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &offset)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR offset\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &nbucket)) {\n      printf (\"ERROR nbucket\\n\");\n      exit (1);\n   }\n\n   nbucket = nbucket + 1;\n   len = len + 1;\n\n   strings = (char*) malloc(n * len);\n\n   for (int i = 0; i < n; i++){\n      if (!fscanf(stdin, \"%s\", strings + (i * len))) {\n      printf (\"ERROR %d\\n\",i);\n      exit (1);\n      }\n   }\n\n   *vString = strings;\n   *N = n;\n   *l = len;\n   *os = offset;\n   *nb = nbucket;\n}\n\nvoid save(char *strings, long int *index, long int n, int len){\n   for (int i = 0; i < n; i++){\n      printf(\"%s\\n\", strings + (index[i] * len));\n   }\n}\n\nint main(int ac, char **av) {\n\n   char     *strings = NULL;\n   long int N        = 0;\n   long int *index   = NULL;\n   int      len      = 0,\n            save2File = 0,\n            offset,\n            nbuckets;\n\n   load(&strings, &N, &len, &offset, &nbuckets);\n\n   index = bucket_sort(strings, len, N, offset, nbuckets);\n\n   save(strings, index, N, len);\n\n   if (strings != NULL)\n      free(strings);\n\n   if (index != NULL)\n      free(index);\n\n   return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/bucketsort.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Stable LSD radix passes should replace the insertion sort's quadratic, loop-carried shifts with work linear in the token count per character, while preserving strcmp ordering and duplicate stability.",
  "notes": "This removes dependence on bucket capacity and orders tokens globally by the same bytewise order as the original buckets for valid inputs. Histogram updates and stable scatter retain real dependencies; no unsafe SIMD directive is added. Correctness and performance remain for the controller to evaluate.",
